# Day 23/60 — Customer & MVP Blueprint

## Overview

Today I used Claude to transform a startup idea into a structured Customer & MVP Blueprint.

The objective was to better understand target customers, identify their pain points, and define a focused MVP roadmap before development.

---

## What Was Generated

- Ideal Customer Profile (ICP)
- Buyer Persona
- Customer Pain Points Analysis
- Customer Journey Map
- Buying Triggers & Objections
- MVP Recommendation
- MoSCoW Prioritization
- Pricing Hypothesis
- Founder Action Plan

---

## Key Learnings

### Customer First, Product Second

A successful product starts with understanding customers rather than building features.

### MVPs Should Stay Small

The first version should solve a core problem effectively rather than trying to do everything.

### Validation Reduces Risk

Customer insights help avoid spending months building features nobody needs.

### AI Accelerates Planning

Claude can act as a customer researcher, product strategist, and startup advisor to generate structured frameworks quickly.

---

## Skills Practiced

- Customer Research
- Product Strategy
- Startup Validation
- MVP Planning
- Business Analysis
- AI-Assisted Decision Making

---

## Biggest Insight

People do not buy products.

They buy solutions to problems.

The better you understand the problem, the better product decisions become.

